  /**
   * <!-- begin-user-doc -->
   * <!-- end-user-doc -->
   * <!-- begin-model-doc -->
   * Summary: Determines whether a customer can book seats on a trip. The trip must exist, the trip must still have enough available seats, the requested seats must not exceed the remaining seats, and the customer must not already hold another booking whose trip time overlaps on the same day. The booking time must be strictly earlier than the departure time by more than two hours, so a booking made exactly two hours before departure is rejected. When the booking is accepted, the trip seat count shall be reduced. Invalid inputs such as a null customer, null trip, or null booking date shall return false.
   * Algorithm:
   *   1. If this.customer is null or this.trip is null or this.bookingDate is null, return false.
   *   2. If this.trip.numberOfSeats - this.trip.getBookedSeats() < this.numberOfSeats, return false.
   *   3. If this.overlapsWith(this.trip) returns true, return false.
   *   4. If this.bookingDate is not strictly more than 2 hours before this.trip.departureTime, return false.
   *   5. Return true.
   * Related Features: customer, trip, bookingDate, numberOfSeats, overlapsWith(trip)
   * Related Classes: Customer, Trip
   * Input: None (uses instance fields: customer, trip, bookingDate, numberOfSeats)
   * Output: boolean - true if booking is eligible, false otherwise
   * Pre-condition: None (null fields return false)
   * Post-condition: If true is returned, this.trip.bookSeats(this.numberOfSeats) is called to reduce seat count.
   * <!-- end-model-doc -->
   * @model kind="operation"
   *        annotation="http://www.ustb.edu.cn/sei/mde/EnhancedCodeGen generated='true'"
   * @generated NOT
   */
